ligence that are feeding  into the foreign secretary if he didn't  seem to be aware of it you are aware of  it and now the whole country knows about  it well it's uh quite clear that there  are two kinds of intelligence failures  there are those failures where the  intelligence agency fails to provide the  intelligence and that's the traditional  meaning of the word and there's a second  kind of intelligence failure where  whoever is the principal didn't read it  i'm afraid you can't blame the spies if  the uh if the officers don't read the  report okay so questions uh further  questions there for the the foreign  secretary um  he didn't seem to have much confidence  about the numbers of people who are  still there who should have been  evacuated he's not in touch with some of  the ambassadors in in third countries  and whose borders that could have been  used to get to get people out and he's  admitted that the afghan staff who were  guarding the uk embassy didn't manage to  get out either  do you think that the foreign office do  you have any confidence in the foreign  office or the foreign secretary  specifically to get those people out  well there's a lot of us uh funnily  enough actually there's a bunch of  ex-military uh folk officers and uh and  other ranks who are currently organizing  to help various individuals um some of  you may have heard that i've one of the  interpreters who worked with me when i  was still serving uh has got stuck i can  i can i'm very pleased to be able to  report that others have got out and  we've had some very good cooperation  with some amazingly dedicated foreign  office personnel in the region and some  extraordinarily courageous uh people  around the world and that has helped us  to get people out i should also say uh  that we've been in pretty regular touch  um with various ministers and um you  know we are able to get some cooperation  and get ministers helping and i'm very  pleased to say that emphasis has been  there so i